=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Identify which sequences are most closely related.
- Recognize the same relationships when branches are rotated.
- Add branch lengths to find the distance between two tips.
- Recognize when a tree leaves the branching order uncertain.

=== layout: two-panels

# *Anniversary of &#8220;On the Origin of Species&#8221;*

@left

- [*Published Nov. 24, 1859*]{color=red}
- Darwin used branching lines to show how species could share ancestors.
- We use branching diagrams to compare the histories of genes and species.

@right

