# Primate Tree

@body

![Original primate tree with saturated orange branches and divergence-time scale](assets/lect11b_restored/primate_tree_saturated.svg)

=== layout: multiple-choice

@speaker-notes

Ask for the choice and the shared ancestor that supports it. Click to reveal only the answer.

@question

![Original primate tree with saturated orange branches and divergence-time scale](assets/lect11b_restored/primate_tree_saturated.svg)

[Which pair of species are the most closely related?]{color=#000000}

- A. gorilla and human
- B. gibbon and gorilla
- C. bonobo and gorilla
- D. bonobo and human

@answer

D. Bonobo and human: shared ancestor 5 million years ago.

=== layout: multiple-choice

@speaker-notes

Ask for the choice and the shared ancestor that supports it. Click to reveal only the answer.

@question

![Original primate tree with saturated orange branches and divergence-time scale](assets/lect11b_restored/primate_tree_saturated.svg)

[Which pair of species are the most closely related?]{color=#000000}

- A. Bornean orangutan and Sumatran orangutan
- B. bonobo and chimpanzee
- C. human and gorilla
- D. gibbon and gorilla

@answer

B. Bonobo and chimpanzee: 2 million years ago. The orangutan pair: 3 million years ago.

=== layout: multiple-choice

@speaker-notes

Ask for the choice and the shared ancestor that supports it. Click to reveal only the answer.

@question

![Original primate tree with saturated orange branches and divergence-time scale](assets/lect11b_restored/primate_tree_saturated.svg)

[When Did Gorillas and Bonobos Share Their Most Recent Common Ancestor?]{color=#000000}

- A. 2 million
- B. 5 million
- C. 7 million
- D. 15 million
- E. 21 million

@answer

C. 7 million years ago, at their shared node.

